## Why This Is Asked
Tests on-device ML design under strict latency, privacy, and fairness constraints; requires end-to-end thinking from data flow to deployment.

## Key Concepts
- Edge ML and latency budgets
- Federated learning with DP
- Model compression (quantization/pruning)
- Fairness-aware ranking
- Rollback and drift monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Latency check scaffold (pseudo)
function measureLatency(model, input){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  model.infer(input);
  const t1 = performance.now();
  return t1 - t0;
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit fairness across departments while maintaining DP guarantees?
- What metrics and rollback triggers would you define for drift detection?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests system design for real-time fraud scoring at scale with privacy constraints, multi-tenant data sharing, and safe rollbacks.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming feature store and time-window features
- Hybrid inference paths: server-side and on-device
- Federated learning with differential privacy
- Drift detection and canary-based rollout strategies
- Model calibration and per-transaction explainability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo scoring sketch
function score(tx, globalModel, localModel){
  const feats = extract(tx)
  const s1 = globalModel.predict(feats)
  const s2 = localModel.predict(feats)
  return calibrate((0.6*s1 + 0.4*s2));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle label latency for online updates?
- What metrics trigger rollback and how would you test rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical baseline ML for streaming signals with delayed labels, focusing on CPU constraints and simple online learning.

## Key Concepts
- Online updates with partial_fit
- Drift detection (PSI/KS)
- Calibration (Platt scaling)
- Simple retraining cadence and data splits

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: batch online update loop
function onlineUpdate(batch){
  model.partial_fit(batch.features, batch.labels);
  monitorDrift(batch.features);
  calibrateIfNeeded();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adjust if latency budget tightens to 50 ms?
- How would you validate calibration over time?
